  "note_uiAssets": "public/ces-ui.css, public/ces-logo.svg and public/ces-favicon.svg are NO LONGER pinned here. They are pushed from the canonical ces-shared/ui/ by the mono-root `npm run sync-ui-assets` (ces/scripts/sync-ui-assets.mjs), which is now muster's drift mechanism for those three files. Pinning them would make every sync fail this check.",
  "note_plannerStores": "2026-09-08 (founder directive): ces-planner's remaining public/data stores (SI/TCP/CUI/BTC/Policy question banks, help guidance, glossary, FedRAMP inheritance table, GCC High G5 tech ref, BTC activation package), its public/schemas output contracts (under public/schemas/planner/) and its policy templates (public/templates/policies/) copied byte-for-byte from ces-planner/public at the same pinned tree (planner untouched since 2026-06-13) so Muster can generate every Planner output. Consume, never fork.",
  "note_evc3": "EVC.3 (2026-10-27): src/vendored/ces-planner/mpt/services/gapCompiler.ts and mpt/types.ts re-copied from ces-mono 81dbc98 (evidence_source / catalog_definitions on Gap, resolveEvidenceArchetypes, compileGapSet arg 9 evidenceCatalog); only the notice Ref and import paths differ (the new type import points at the vendored shared/services/evidenceCatalog.ts). Re-pinned.",
  "note_evidenceCatalog": "EVC.1 (2026-10-27): the evidence catalog data (release log, release 0 = AC 3.1.1 example, NIST 800-171A examine lists, objective coverage buckets) copied byte-for-byte from ../ces-planner/public/data/evidence-catalog/ into src/vendored/ces-planner/data/evidence-catalog/ (Muster public/ is not used for it), plus the Planner seed loader (only import paths and the notice Ref differ). The ces-shared schema and types are imported from the ces-shared package (ces-shared/data/evidence-catalog-schema, ces-shared/types/evidence-catalog) since DUP-4a. To refresh the Planner-sourced files: copy them again, re-pin here, run check:drift --against-sibling. Pins for these seven files were taken from the ces-mono working copy ahead of its commit (HEAD 71f919e at the time), not at verifiedAgainst.commit.",
  "note_dup4a": "DUP-4a (2026-10-30, GAP-CLOSURE-PLAN.md G-DUP): Muster depends on ces-shared directly. ces-muster/package.json has \"ces-shared\": \"file:../ces-shared\" and muster-api/package.json has \"file:../../ces-shared\"; imports use the subpath exports in ces-shared/package.json. src/vendored/ces-shared and muster-api/src/vendored/ces-shared were deleted (14 pins removed), with src/vendored/cesSharedSync.ts, its parity test and the check:ces-shared / sync:ces-shared scripts. After DUP-4a this manifest pinned ces-planner, ces-spine and other non-ces-shared copies only.",
  "note_dup4b": "DUP-4b (2026-10-30, GAP-CLOSURE-PLAN.md G-DUP): Planner code is no longer vendored. All 59 files of src/vendored/ces-planner were still used (transitive closure from Muster importers), so all moved: mpt/services/gapCompiler.ts to src/features/gaps/gapCompiler.ts, everything else (code and the evidence-catalog data) to src/features/plan/engine/ with the same sub-paths. muster-api/src/vendored/ces-planner/mpt/services/validator.ts moved to muster-api/src/services/artifactAlignmentValidator.ts. 60 pins removed; the moved files are Muster-owned code now, not drift-checked copies. Still pinned from ces-planner (plannerPinnedSha): public/knowledge, public/schemas/planner, public/templates/policies, src/__fixtures__/builders.ts and the exportPlanShim.ts shim; ces-spine is unchanged.",
